   "book": "dumnealui / dumneaei / dumnealor",
   "spoken": "el / ea / ei — or dânsul / dânsa",
   "gloss": "he / she / they (respectful)",
   "note": "The book's dumnealui, dumneaei, dumnealor are correct and genuinely polite, but formal — for a superior, an elderly person, an office. In ordinary talk el and ea are neutral and fine for most people. 'Dânsul / dânsa' is a common middle-politeness option in Romania, though some treat it as regional. With a stranger, dumnealui/dumneaei is never wrong.",
   "confidence": "check"
  },
