   "gloss": "house vs. flat",
   "note": "'Acasă' means home, wherever that is — but most city people live in an 'apartament' in a 'bloc' (an apartment building), not a detached 'casă'. 'Casă' still doubles as home/household in fixed phrases (la mine acasă), so 'merg acasă' is 'I'm going home' even when home is a flat.",
